#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434834} :activity/id #uuid "67831f4f-8138-536f-9514-23aeb5868445" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/id #uuid "8698dcb0-d732-5f62-8605-520598e45185" :topic/math-academy-id 4145} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434832 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b1374a-677b-550b-816a-6cbd02c5f061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434818} {:answer/id #uuid "29ead56c-2949-5fb0-8895-cdd6a87df4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3bf5e7-fb1f-5845-863a-15bfb2564e17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434824} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e03b7e-e933-5e07-a534-f79399c89baf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434825} {:answer/id #uuid "c757d8e1-3c0b-5fc9-9360-e929a186b1fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434826}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1855324-ee18-529c-ba15-53c93565cb17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "22bda1b7-731c-5be9-8f1b-6668d9e068b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161253" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =v\\cdot 2u+uv\\cdot (-1)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2uv-uv+0 \\\\  & =uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot uv+0\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+0=1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "764dfadc-7353-5f72-bb5e-9db6eccbfeca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434833}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434833 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4ed277-51d3-5190-9f15-e73dd884cf47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} {:answer/id #uuid "471dabbc-d133-52dc-b559-394801c709a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434821} {:answer/id #uuid "777af6b2-9aef-5099-aac7-98b1ec37120e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434822} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1f231c-84b6-5409-b4c5-4c9196b18b4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434823} {:answer/id #uuid "de47629f-21da-52b1-941b-ae2f3625cecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434827}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434819} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1a0c12-6b57-5589-b4e1-416cdc457a68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434828}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5815497-10bb-5d31-b1ef-c78b6eb79a17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161259" :question/problem "Evaluate the surface integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere the parametric surface $S$ is defined by\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain $D=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.$\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe're given that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & ={⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩|}_{x=u+v\\,y=v-u\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u+v,\\,v-u,\\,-uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-u-v,\\,v-u,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-u-v)+(v-u)\\cdot (v-u)+(-uv)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-2uv-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-2uv+{u}^{2}-2uv \\\\  & =-6uv\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral evaluates to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\,y,\\,-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6uv)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}uv\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{1}v\\,\\text{d}v{\\int }_{-2}^{0}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-6\\cdot [\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2}]_{0}^{1}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9468f911-b5bd-557b-9a6f-8e025c4a65c6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434834 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194750cf-4b33-5153-97c1-bd1b0f21c3c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275713} {:answer/id #uuid "30772c46-8461-5daa-94aa-ff5b8a754f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275909} {:answer/id #uuid "45100deb-1ec8-5bbb-b0b4-3c26c5616332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2u{v}^{3}+4{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276086} {:answer/id #uuid "45e6001c-4deb-5a8c-b01f-01531e4489d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4u{v}^{3}+2{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276094} {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81d9840-6037-5557-81d1-599235b0ea5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e88e2f68-fd58-50c1-9108-060ce4b3171a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434832}}] :activity/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434817}]}
